rs at the lowest probability in each lottery, then in Lottery A, the lowest probability (10%) is linked to 0 Euros, so the most favorable outcome at that probability is 0. In Lottery B, the lowest probability (45%) is linked to 6000 Euros, so the most favorable outcome at that probability is 6000. Therefore, Lottery B has a more favorable outcome (6000) at its minimum probability, while Lottery A has 0 at its minimum probability. Hence, the reason would prefer Lottery B. The information required by the reason can be derived from the lotteries: the minimum probability and the associated outcome for each lottery. So the reason is applicable.",
